# Stage 7 sketch — wheel-sync / fault-recovery verification log (29.10, desk)

> Scope: the ADDITIVE fault layer in `lab1_stage7_faultrecovery.ino` (stage 6
> source + fault layer; stage 6 files untouched). Blocks 1–2: host-side only
> (MSYS2 g++ vs the virtual-robot harness) — hardware was still pending at
> that time (closed 30.10, see the REAL-ROBOT block at the end). All numbers
> in the sim blocks are real tool output, suite exit codes checked.

## 1. Compile

- host g++ (MSYS2, -Wall -Wextra), sketch + sim_fault.cpp: the ONLY warning is
  the pre-existing `wheelTargetMM unused` (same warning exists for the frozen
  stage6 sketch — verified, not introduced by stage 7).
- regression suites recompiled clean against the touched harness.

## 2. Harness changes (_hostcheck/Arduino.h — additive, defaults preserve frozen behaviour)

1. `SLIP_L/SLIP_R` (default 0): per-wheel traction-loss injection. Ground
   motion scales by (1-slip), encoder ticks by (1 + slip*(SLIP_FREE_GAIN-1)):
   slip UNLOADS the motor, disc free-spins ~5x (stage-1 bench: 292 free vs
   59 loaded cnt/s at pwm 130, data.txt). Zero default = bit-identical plant.
2. `MAX_MM_S` became a runtime knob (default 300, the frozen nominal). ONLY
   sim_fault sets 592.0 — the floor-calibrated value (stage-2/3 map: pwm 130 →
   302 mm/s under load, which the sketch's PWM_PER_MMS is built on). First
   attempt made it a global constant: stage4/5/wheelstop suites broke (they are
   calibrated on the nominal plant) — reverted, knob pattern chosen instead.
3. `simMicrosBump`: sub-tick micros spacing for inline edges, ACTIVE ONLY WHEN
   SLIP_L/SLIP_R > 0. Without it the ISR's 800 µs debounce ate every second
   back-to-back edge of a free-spinning disc (slip rate landed ON the detector
   threshold — flaky pass/fail). Gated so normal-speed counting stays
   bit-identical to the frozen suites' calibration.

## 3. Sketch design delta vs stage 6 (all inside the straight path; turnStep untouched)

- constants: 12 new #define-style tunables (see REPORT_STAGE7.md sec.2).
- MotState gains M_HOLD. controlStep(): windowed detectors run FIRST:
  1. one-wheel stall = RELATIVE ratio over 80 ms windows (guard-v2 pattern:
     healthy <= 7 %, firm hold <= 13 %, threshold 20 %, partner >= 3 cnt),
     3 consecutive windows -> brake() BOTH + M_HOLD. Chosen over an absolute
     quiet-count threshold after the first sim run: absolute thresholds are
     plant-specific (the nominal plant put pwm 85 at ~100 mm/s = stall-like);
     the ratio detector is plant-independent and floor-proven.
  2. both-wheels-dead windows -> `err: drive blocked` abort (the stage-6
     STALL_MS watchdog only covers never-started: it refreshes on ANY count).
  3. slip rate |d(cL-cR)|/100 ms > 8 cnt -> latch: progress = MIN(|cL|,|cR|),
     corr = 0. Slip ALSO caught by the sustained detector (|diff| >= 20 mm for
     2 windows) for slow leaks.
- M_HOLD: alternating fwd/rev test pulses (110 pwm < 120 breakaway, yaw
  cancels), 2-pulse cycles judge the stuck wheel; freed x2 cycles -> RESYNC:
  progress := MIN(|cL|,|cR|), symmetry reference := post-event difference,
  resume ORIGINAL target; 3 countless cycles -> abort. c/b abort from hold,
  fresh G/L/R re-commands, S = last-fault record, p shows hold state.
- spool grace 400 ms (or 10 counts moved) after start/resync: motor spool-up
  yields <= ~2.5 cnt/80 ms which the ratio window cannot judge — without the
  grace every drive aborted at t=240 ms (found in the first sim run).
- protocol: only ADDITIONS (S key, M_HOLD state, hold/clear/abort lines).
  G/L/R/K/J/m/c/b/t/e/z/s/p/x/h/? semantics unchanged; done/go/tturn format
  unchanged; queue held frozen during hold (a queued command must not fight
  the fault latch; a fresh typed G bypasses = re-command path).

## 4. sim_fault.cpp — 29 checks, fails=0, exit 0

| scenario | checks | verdict |
|---|---|---|
| S1 healthy G0.5 + S key state=none | 4 | done, got=495.5, poseX=498.0, NO false fault |
| S2 one-wheel stall mid-drive -> hold -> resync | 7 | warn names L, MIN progress banked (~100 mm), sync line, NO yaw from pulses (poseY -2.8 mm), completes ORIGINAL 600 mm target (got=592.6) |
| S3 hand-hold WITH jerk edges (guard-v1 killer) | 2 | detected via windowed displacement; c aborts cleanly from hold |
| S4 re-command during hold (fresh G0.3) | 3 | go accepted, fresh drive completes (got=291.2) |
| S5 both wheels freeze mid-drive | 4 | `err: drive blocked` abort, drift 0.57 mm (braked, not coast), recovery drive completes |
| S6 full breakaway slip on L (5x free-spin) | 5 | rate warn fires, completes on MIN-progress (got=490.4, ground 77 mm), no overshoot from fake counts, S key names the slip |
| S7 S key after faults | 1 | record printed |
| S8 turn regression L90 | 3 | tturn completes, got=79.5 vs stage6-reference 77.5 (band 75-80 = the frozen turn machine's own sim kick-fold spread, verified by running the FROZEN stage6 binary in the same harness), no fault output in turns |

