## 6. Honest limits

- Sim-only at the time of writing. The hold/resync cycle, pulse PWM (110 vs the
  ~120 breakaway) and the slip thresholds are tuned against bench/free-spin
  numbers; the real confirmation is the REPORT_STAGE7.md sec.5 test plan
  (hold a wheel during G0.6; dust-sheet slip run; grab test).
  -> CLOSED 30.10: real-robot session done, see the REAL-ROBOT block at the
  end of this log and REPORT_STAGE7.md sec.5.1.
- SLIP_DIFF_MAX_CNT 8 is derived from CORR_MAX_DRV + 6 % motor asym on the
  calibrated map; on the real floor verify with the telemetry line during a
  deliberate dust run before trusting the latch.
- The stage3 working copy (wheel-guard v2, uncommitted) is untouched; stage 7
  is a parallel implementation on the stage6 base with the same detector
  philosophy but hold+resync instead of abort semantics.

