summary (full analysis in REPORT_STAGE7.md sec.5.1):
- accuracy: +1.4 / -3.7 mm on 5000 mm (mean -1.15 mm = -0.023 %,
  |err| mean 2.55 mm = 0.051 %) — both inside ONE STOP_TOL_MM (10 mm)
- recovery: 7/7 stall-holds cleared and resumed on the ORIGINAL target;
  clear durations operator-driven (1680 ms = design minimum,
  HOLD_CLR_WINDOWS x (HOLD_TEST_MS+HOLD_GAP_MS)); 7 slip latches, no
  counter-chasing
- abort: attempt 2 escalated via the both-wheels-dead detector
  (N_STALL_STEPS x STALL_WIN_MS = 3 x 80 ms = 240 ms of zero output) —
  CORRECT safety behaviour, not a regression (sim S5 analogue)
- consistency: resume-point chains close to the final got= in both
  completed runs; done-line got= is slip-safe MIN-progress minus the
  recaptured symmetry reference, not the raw wheel mean (expected)

